course: dictionary
lesson: 4897
title: Ill and its many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. Ill most often means sick, not well: «He is ill in bed.» Read the words around it to choose the right meaning. A bed and rest are clues that it means sick.
explain: Ill can also mean bad or harmful, as in «ill effects». It can mean badly, as in «ill-treated», and it can be a noun, «ills», meaning problems or troubles. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then put your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: When you feel ill, tell a trusted adult, rest, drink water and stay home so you do not spread germs. Only take medicine that a trusted adult gives you.
explain: Ill also appears in phrases. Ill at ease means uncomfortable, and ill-mannered means rude. These phrases do not always mean sick, so look at the whole sentence.
fact: Ill means sick, not well.
fact: Ill can also mean bad or harmful, as in «ill effects».
fact: As an adverb, ill means badly, as in «ill-treated».
fact: The noun «ills» means problems or troubles.
fact: Ill at ease means feeling uncomfortable.
exercise: «He is ill in bed.» What does ill mean here? | Bad or harmful | *Sick, not well | Full of problems | Badly, in an unkind way
exercise: «The ill effects of the storm lasted for days.» What does ill mean here? | Happy and bright | *Bad or harmful | Sick, not well | Badly, in an unkind way
exercise: «One kind act, like bringing soup to someone ill, can end a feud.» What does ill mean here? | Full of troubles | *Sick, not well | Badly treated
test: «Vultures have strong stomach acid that kills germs that would make other animals ill.» What does ill mean here? | Badly and unfairly | Problems or troubles | *Sick, not well | Bad or harmful to the ground
test: «The town had many ills, such as broken roads and dirty streets.» What does ills mean here? | *Problems or troubles | Happy times | Bad smells | Sick people
exam: Which sentence uses ill as a noun meaning problems? | «He felt ill after lunch.» | «The children were ill at ease in the new school.» | *«Money worries are one of the ills that families can face.» | «She was ill-treated by the crowd.»
